# OpenClaw setup should inject SERPER_API_KEY through skills.entries.
# For direct CLI compatibility only, create config/serper.env once without
# truncating an existing file:
#   (umask 077; set -o noclobber; : > config/serper.env)
# Then edit it locally. Never rerun creation for an existing file, and never
# commit that file.
# The loader also requires a regular non-symlink file owned by the current user
# or root, exactly one hard link, and a maximum size of 16 KiB.
#
# Preferred standard env-style format:
SERPER_API_KEY=your_serper_api_key_here
#
# Optional compatibility format understood by the loader:
# Key: your_serper_api_key_here
#
# Direct CLI users may add multiple lines. The loader rotates those keys, but
# OpenClaw's standard primaryEnv/API-key injection supplies one key per run.
# For environment-only multi-key use, SERPER_API_KEYS accepts comma/newline
# separators. Do not put a SERPER_API_KEYS= assignment in this file.
